  We end this section with the following lemma, which is useful in the analysis of one-dimensional faces. It will be used repeatedly in our subsequent discussions.
  \begin{lemma}[{\cite[Lemma 2.5]{LiLoPo21}}]
	\label{lemma:Lemma-2.11}
	Let \( \stdCone \) be a pointed closed convex cone and let \( \bm{z}\in \partial \stdCone^*\setminus \{{\bm 0}\} \) be such that \( \stdFace := \{\bm{z}\}^{\perp} \cap \stdCone \) is a one-dimensional proper face of \( \stdCone \).
	Let \( \bm{f} \in \stdCone \setminus \{\bm{0}\} \) be such that \( \stdFace = \{t \bm{f} \, | \, t \geq 0\} \).
